// Ambient sound: what the world sounds like where the player is (see client/src/ambience).
//
// groups: kinds of block counted around the player by a flood fill from the eye, nearer
//   ones counting more (10 within 5 blocks, 5 within 10, 2 within 15, 1 up to 24). Each
//   group is selected by block tags or materials (`falling: true`: only fluid pouring
//   down; `lit: true`: a structure's core only while its fire burns) and is an axis of its
//   own, 0 below the first number of its range and 1 above the second. A block counts for
//   the first group that selects it. A group that `cools: ("kiln", 120)` selects nothing of
//   its own: it counts a lit group's cores for that many seconds (at most 600) after their
//   fire goes out, as the client saw it go.
// beds: continuous layers, synthesized (`sound`) or recorded (`recording`: three segments in
//   this package, eight seconds each, fading in and out over their first and last second
//   and a half, as the mixer crossfades them). `volume` at full strength; `when` holds soft ranges on axes,
//   each full between `min` and `max` and fading out over `fade` beyond them; `biome` and
//   `not_biome` want or avoid biome tags; `duck` turns the bed down by an axis or another
//   bed (0.8: to a fifth at its fullest); `fade` is the seconds to fade fully in or out.
// roofs: rain on the roof overhead. The roof is the lowest solid block (not leaves) within
//   `height` blocks above the head of any column the player's body passed beneath since the
//   last look (four looks a second). Its material (a building material of sounds.ron, else
//   its family sound: stone, wood, soil, ...) names a `patter`, or None for silence; every
//   roof material must have an entry, or the game does not start. Each patter is an axis,
//   the rain falling while under a roof of it, for beds to play on. Under any roof the
//   `sheltered` axis is `muffle`, and a roof block of a patter in `patter_shelter` muffles
//   that much more of what is left, else one with a `shelter` tag does (each block muffles
//   the rain once); the open rain ducks under it, and so do the wind, storms, fields
//   and shore outside, so a home is a quiet place to be.
// draughts: each draughty shelter tag names the beds its walls whistle with when the wind
//   finds their gaps. Each bed must play on a group counting that tag, so the more of
//   those walls near the louder, and none (every cell daubed) is silence. Every `shelter:`
//   tag a block has must be in `roofs.shelter` or here, or the game does not start.
// sounds: one-shots, played `per_minute` times a minute while their conditions fully hold,
//   then not again for `cooldown` seconds. `at` is Block(group) (a block the scan found),
//   OpenBlock(group) (one of those with nothing over it but the sky; none, not heard),
//   Around(distance, height) or Listener. `reach` is the distance (blocks) at which they
//   are half as loud; `pitch` the range of playback speed.
//
// Axes: air (0 enclosed .. 1 open land), sky (share of nearby air open to the sky),
// canopy (share of that under leaves), reverb (0 outdoors .. 1 large cave), sun (-1
// midnight .. 1 noon), temperature (°C), moisture, continentalness (-1 ocean, 0 coast, 1
// inland), river (1 by a river or lake), flowing (by running water only), still (by a lake
// or spring only), forest, height (above sea), relief (above the land around), depth
// (below the ground surface here), rain (heard falling, less under a roof), raining
// (falling at all), wetness (of the ground), snow, storm (0..1), wind (blocks/s, gusts
// included), gusts (how gusty, 0..1), hail, sleet, dust (0..1, as heard here), cover,
// underwater, shelter (0 outdoors .. 1 indoors: a roof overhead and walls around, a door
// open or not; caves too, not trees), roof (a roof close overhead the sky falls on, walls
// or not), settlement (blocks to the middle of the nearest settlement, 10000 with none
// within 192), settlement_edge (blocks outside the nearest settlement's bounds, the ground
// its buildings stand on and six blocks round, 0 within, 10000 with none), settlement_people
// (how many live there: its size), sheltered (how much a roof overhead muffles the open
// rain), home (how far up `home`'s ladder the player stands), the groups below, the
// roof patters, and `effect:NAME` for any effect (effects.ron): 1 while the player holds
// it, else 0, so a home is heard as the server judged it (a door shut, an evening in).
// Each must be an effect, or the game does not start.
//
// home: the home ladder's effects (effects.ron), lowest first: the `home` axis is 0 away
//   from home, 1 holding the first, 2 the second, and so on, by the highest held. Each
//   must be an effect, or the game does not start; a later package's list replaces it.
//
// shelter: how indoors is told and heard. `walls`: blocks from the eye a wall may be and
//   count; `roof`: blocks above it a roof may be for the `roof` axis; `muffle`: Hz an outdoor
//   one-shot is muffled down to fully indoors (a layer is outdoor when it ducks by
//   `shelter`, and one-shots are muffled as far as they duck); `thunder`: how loud thunder
//   is fully indoors, against out in the open. A layer ducks by both: `sheltered` for the
//   roof over it (by what the roof is made of), `shelter` for the walls round it as well.
(
    // Indoors is cozy: the weather and the wild outside fall to a murmur through the walls,
    // the rain drums on the roof, and the hearth crackles clear (fire layers never duck by
    // shelter).
    shelter: (walls: 6, roof: 8, muffle: 700, thunder: 0.5),
    // The home ladder: a camp, a lit hearth, roofed and walled (Snug), then the Farm age's
    // homes, each cosier than the last.
    home: ["camp", "hearthside", "snug", "homely", "cosy", "heart_of_the_home"],
    groups: [
        // Walls that let the wind through, as the home judges a room's walls (`shelter`:
        // a `shelter:draughty` block such as wattle or hide, or earth, gravel, sand and any
        // other solid block with no shelter tag, until daub coats it; never the floor, nor
        // furniture). Counted beside a block's own group, never instead. A few draughty cells
        // within five blocks begin to whistle; a room walled in them whistles fully.
        (name: "draughty", shelter: Draughty, range: (10, 160)),
        // Curtains drawn across (`curtain_drawn`): cloth over the gaps hushes the draught's
        // whistle, half with one near, all with two.
        (name: "curtained", tags: ["curtain_drawn"], range: (0, 20)),
        // Thatch or wattle smouldering by a flame, about to catch (fire.ron): heard only while
        // it smoulders (`smouldering`), one within a few blocks fully.
        (name: "smoulder", tags: ["thatch", "wattle"], range: (1, 4), smouldering: true),
        // Thatch or wattle burning (fire.ron's `burning` block): each burning cell near counts,
        // so the crackle is fullest while the fire runs through a roof and thins as cell after
        // cell burns out to ash. Four within five blocks fully.
        (name: "blaze", tags: ["blaze"], range: (0, 40)),
        (name: "leaves", tags: ["leaves"], range: (20, 300)),
        (name: "wood", tags: ["log"], range: (5, 60)),
        // Boards: a timber floor, walls and roof (`planks`), as a home is built of them.
        (name: "timber", tags: ["planks"], range: (20, 200)),
        // A Crucible Kiln firing (its core, heard only while its fire burns): before the
        // fire, so it roars as a kiln, not a hearth. Fully within five blocks.
        (name: "kiln", tags: ["crucible"], range: (3, 10), lit: true),
        // A charcoal clamp smouldering (its flue, `clamp_burning`): logs charring under the soil.
        (name: "clamp", tags: ["clamp_burning"], range: (1, 4)),
        // A fire to sit by: a campfire, a hearth, a pit kiln. Before rock, as a hearthstone
        // or a kiln is stone to the step. One within five blocks is a fire fully heard; by
        // ten blocks it has faded to a murmur, and past fifteen it is gone. `lit`: a hearth
        // (a structure's core) is heard only while its fire burns.
        (name: "fire", tags: ["campfire", "hearth", "pit_kiln"], range: (3, 10), lit: true),
        // A kiln or a hearth just gone out (the server no longer says it burns): its bricks
        // or stones ticking as they cool, the kiln's for two minutes, a hearth's for one. They
        // select no blocks of their own: the cores of the lit group named, cooling.
        (name: "kiln_cooling", cools: ("kiln", 120), range: (1, 4)),
        (name: "fire_cooling", cools: ("fire", 60), range: (1, 4)),
        // Lava and falling water sound like water to the step, so they come first.
        (name: "lava", tags: ["lava"], range: (4, 80)),
        // A pot on the boil (`simmering`): one within five blocks is full.
        (name: "pot", tags: ["simmering"], range: (2, 10)),
        // A window in the wall (`window`: glass, oiled hide, a lattice, shutters open); shut
        // shutters are none. A window or two near counts fully.
        (name: "window", tags: ["window"], range: (0, 2)),
        (name: "falls", materials: [Water], falling: true, range: (6, 90)),
        (name: "water", materials: [Water], range: (20, 300)),
        // Bees at a skep or a wild nest (`bees`): one close by is heard fully.
        (name: "hive", tags: ["bees"], range: (1, 6)),
        // Not heard: the air's pollen keeps near flowers (client/src/weather/atmosphere.rs).
        // Before grass, as a block counts for the first group that selects it.
        (name: "flowers", tags: ["flower"], range: (4, 60)),
        (name: "grass", materials: [Grass], range: (150, 1200)),
        (name: "rock", materials: [Stone, Gravel], range: (60, 700)),
        (name: "sand", materials: [Sand], range: (60, 600)),
        (name: "snowpack", materials: [Snow], range: (60, 600)),
        // Ice: a frozen pond or lake, a glacier's edge.
        (name: "ice", tags: ["ice"], range: (20, 300)),
    ],
    roofs: (
        height: 12,
        muffle: 0.45,
        // A sound or fine roof keeps out more of the rain's noise than a draughty one, when
        // what it is made of does not already say (`patter_shelter`).
        shelter: {"shelter:sound": 0.3, "shelter:fine": 0.5},
        // And what the roof is made of: thatch and turf hush the rain, shingles and boards
        // keep out a fair share, stone and brick most; glass little. Not a roof with a
        // `draughty` tag (a lean-to, open at its sides), which keeps only `muffle`.
        patter_shelter: {"roof_soft": 0.3, "roof_tap": 0.3, "roof_dull": 0.5, "roof_bright": 0.1},
        draughty: ["shelter:draughty"],
        patter: {
            // Soft: straw, hide, turf and earth take the drops in.
            "thatch": "roof_soft", "hide": "roof_soft", "soil": "roof_soft", "grass": "roof_soft", "mud": "roof_soft", "moss": "roof_soft", "sand": "roof_soft",
            // A tap: shingles, boards, timber, woven withies and fired tiles.
            "shingle": "roof_tap", "timber": "roof_tap", "wood": "roof_tap", "wattle": "roof_tap", "terracotta": "roof_tap", "cradle": "roof_tap",
            // Dull: stone, brick, gravel and clay daub.
            "stone": "roof_dull", "cobblestone": "roof_dull", "stone_brick": "roof_dull", "gravel": "roof_dull", "daub": "roof_dull",
            // Bright: glass.
            "glass": "roof_bright",
            // Snow takes rain in without a sound; water and leaves are never roofs.
            "snow": None, "water": None, "leaves": None,
        },
    ),
    draughts: {"shelter:draughty": ["draught", "draught_rain"]},
    beds: [
        // A draughty home at night: under a roof (`sheltered`), by walls that let the wind
        // through, a thin whistle in the gusts, louder the more such walls are near, hushed
        // by curtains drawn across (`curtained`); on a
        // wet night with little wind, a fainter one. Daubing the wattle stops it.
        (
            name: "draught", sound: Draught, volume: 0.22, fade: 4,
            when: {"draughty": (min: 1, fade: 0.95), "sheltered": (min: 0.35, fade: 0.2), "wind": (min: 7, fade: 5), "sun": (max: 0.05, fade: 0.15), "curtained": (max: 0, fade: 1)},
        ),
        (
            name: "draught_rain", sound: Draught, volume: 0.12, fade: 4,
            when: {"draughty": (min: 1, fade: 0.95), "sheltered": (min: 0.35, fade: 0.2), "raining": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.2), "sun": (max: 0.05, fade: 0.15), "curtained": (max: 0, fade: 1)},
            duck: {"draught": 1},
        ),
        // Rain, recorded (CC0; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) and layered the AmbientSounds
        // way. Out in the open, a patter on leaves and ground that grows with the rain, then
        // gives way to the roar of a downpour; under a roof close overhead, indoors or on a
        // porch, the drumming on it; under trees while they are wet, drops falling from the
        // leaves. With the door shut (`door_shut`) the rain and wind outside drop away further,
        // and the drum on the roof carries on.
        (
            name: "rain", recording: ["sounds/rain_light_1.mp3", "sounds/rain_light_2.mp3", "sounds/rain_light_3.mp3"], volume: 0.5, fade: 3,
            when: {"rain": (min: 0.45, max: 0.75, fade: 0.42)},
            duck: {"hail": 0.7, "sleet": 0.4, "sheltered": 1, "shelter": 0.75, "effect:door_shut": 0.5},
        ),
        (
            name: "downpour", recording: ["sounds/rain_heavy_1.mp3", "sounds/rain_heavy_2.mp3", "sounds/rain_heavy_3.mp3"], volume: 0.75, fade: 3,
            when: {"rain": (min: 0.85, fade: 0.4)},
            duck: {"hail": 0.7, "sheltered": 1, "shelter": 0.75, "effect:door_shut": 0.5},
        ),
        // Rain on the roof overhead, by what it is made of (`roofs`), heard near the surface
        // (not through the rock over a cave).
        (
            name: "rain_on_roof", recording: ["sounds/rain_roof_1.mp3", "sounds/rain_roof_2.mp3", "sounds/rain_roof_3.mp3"], volume: 0.4, fade: 2,
            when: {"roof_tap": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.25), "depth": (max: 4, fade: 3)},
        ),
        (
            name: "rain_on_thatch", sound: ThatchPatter, volume: 0.35, fade: 2,
            when: {"roof_soft": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.25), "depth": (max: 4, fade: 3)},
        ),
        (
            name: "rain_on_stone", sound: StonePatter, volume: 0.35, fade: 2,
            when: {"roof_dull": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.25), "depth": (max: 4, fade: 3)},
        ),
        (
            name: "rain_on_glass", sound: GlassPatter, volume: 0.3, fade: 2,
            when: {"roof_bright": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.25), "depth": (max: 4, fade: 3)},
        ),
        (
            name: "dripping_trees", recording: ["sounds/drips_1.mp3", "sounds/drips_2.mp3", "sounds/drips_3.mp3"], volume: 0.35, fade: 8,
            when: {"wetness": (min: 0.45, fade: 0.3), "leaves": (min: 0.35, fade: 0.3), "air": (min: 0.05, fade: 0.1)},
            duck: {"shelter": 0.8, "downpour": 0.8},
        ),
        // A soft breeze anywhere outdoors, stronger with the wind.
        (
            name: "breeze", sound: Wind, volume: 0.2,
            when: {"sky": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.4), "air": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.3), "wind": (min: 8, fade: 12)},
            duck: {"sheltered": 1, "rain": 0.5, "high_wind": 0.7, "shelter": 0.85, "effect:door_shut": 0.5},
        ),
        // Wind on peaks and ridges, and in storms.
        (
            name: "high_wind", sound: Gale, volume: 0.4, fade: 6,
            when: {"relief": (min: 30, fade: 25), "sky": (min: 0.6, fade: 0.3), "wind": (min: 10, fade: 14)},
            duck: {"sheltered": 1, "shelter": 0.8, "effect:door_shut": 0.5},
        ),
        (
            name: "storm_wind", sound: Gale, volume: 0.32,
            when: {"storm": (min: 0.6, fade: 0.5), "sky": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.4)},
            duck: {"sheltered": 1, "shelter": 0.75, "effect:door_shut": 0.5},
        ),
        // Ice falling: hail rattling on everything, sleet's fine patter.
        (
            name: "hail", recording: ["sounds/hail_1.mp3", "sounds/hail_2.mp3", "sounds/hail_3.mp3"], volume: 0.55, fade: 2,
            when: {"hail": (min: 0.25, fade: 0.25)},
            duck: {"sheltered": 0.5, "shelter": 0.6, "effect:door_shut": 0.4},
        ),
        (
            name: "sleet", sound: Sleet, volume: 0.3, fade: 3,
            when: {"sleet": (min: 0.2, fade: 0.2)},
            duck: {"sheltered": 0.6, "shelter": 0.7, "effect:door_shut": 0.4},
        ),
        // Sand and dust driven by a strong wind.
        (
            name: "sandstorm", sound: Sandstorm, volume: 0.45, fade: 4,
            when: {"dust": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.35)},
            duck: {"sheltered": 0.7, "rain": 0.5, "shelter": 0.8},
        ),
        // Snow driven hard: a blizzard's howl.
        (
            name: "blizzard", sound: Gale, volume: 0.36, fade: 5,
            when: {"snow": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.3), "wind": (min: 8, fade: 6), "sky": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.4)},
            duck: {"sheltered": 1, "shelter": 0.75},
        ),
        // Leaves in the breeze, under and among trees.
        (
            name: "leaves", sound: Rustle, volume: 0.24,
            when: {"leaves": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.4), "sky": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.4), "wind": (min: 6, fade: 10)},
            duck: {"sheltered": 0.6, "rain": 0.6, "high_wind": 0.5, "shelter": 0.85},
        ),
        // Grasshoppers on a mild or warm day in open grassland. Temperatures are yearly
        // means, so insects sing from fairly cool climates up.
        (
            name: "meadow", sound: Meadow, volume: 0.16,
            when: {"grass": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.4), "sun": (min: 0.15, fade: 0.15), "temperature": (min: 10, fade: 6), "sky": (min: 0.7, fade: 0.3), "leaves": (max: 0.15, fade: 0.25)},
            not_biome: ["desert", "frozen"],
            duck: {"sheltered": 0.8, "rain": 0.9, "high_wind": 0.6, "hail": 0.95, "sleet": 0.9, "dust": 0.95, "shelter": 0.85},
        ),
        // Crickets on warm nights wherever there is grass or trees.
        (
            name: "crickets", sound: Crickets, volume: 0.12, fade: 8,
            when: {"sun": (max: -0.1, fade: 0.1), "temperature": (min: 9, fade: 6), "grass": (min: 0.35, fade: 0.3), "sky": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.4)},
            not_biome: ["desert", "frozen"],
            duck: {"sheltered": 0.6, "rain": 0.9, "high_wind": 0.6, "hail": 0.95, "sleet": 0.9, "dust": 0.95, "shelter": 0.75},
        ),
        // Running water, recorded: a creek's babble, louder the more the place is by the
        // water (a wide fade on `flowing`, so it grows from the edge of the valley in).
        (
            name: "stream", recording: ["sounds/brook_1.mp3", "sounds/brook_2.mp3", "sounds/brook_3.mp3"], volume: 0.45,
            when: {"water": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.25), "flowing": (min: 0.9, fade: 0.6), "air": (min: 0.05, fade: 0.1)},
            duck: {"shelter": 0.75, "rain": 0.4, "downpour": 0.5},
        ),
        // Small waves lapping at the shore of a lake.
        (
            name: "lake", recording: ["sounds/lake_1.mp3", "sounds/lake_2.mp3", "sounds/lake_3.mp3"], volume: 0.35, fade: 5,
            when: {"water": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.3), "still": (min: 0.7, fade: 0.45), "air": (min: 0.05, fade: 0.1)},
            duck: {"shelter": 0.75, "rain": 0.5, "high_wind": 0.4},
        ),
        // Surf on the coast.
        (
            name: "surf", sound: Surf, volume: 0.36, fade: 6,
            when: {"water": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.4), "continentalness": (max: 0.05, fade: 0.15), "height": (max: 12, fade: 25), "sky": (min: 0.4, fade: 0.4)},
            duck: {"sheltered": 0.4, "rain": 0.3, "shelter": 0.75},
        ),
        // The still air of caves, recorded in a quarry tunnel: a slight room tone with drips
        // far off. Wet rock: under a moderate climate or wetter (moisture 0.75 and up), fading
        // to dry rock's own, below, under dry lands and deserts (0.45 and down).
        (
            name: "cave", recording: ["sounds/cave_1.mp3", "sounds/cave_2.mp3", "sounds/cave_3.mp3"], volume: 0.45, fade: 5,
            when: {"sky": (max: 0.05, fade: 0.15), "depth": (min: 5, fade: 4), "air": (min: 0.02, fade: 0.05), "moisture": (min: 0.75, fade: 0.3)},
        ),
        // Dry rock: the low, still air of a cave with no water in it, a faint draught and
        // nothing dripping.
        (
            name: "dry_cave", sound: Cave, volume: 0.4, fade: 5,
            when: {"sky": (max: 0.05, fade: 0.15), "depth": (min: 5, fade: 4), "air": (min: 0.02, fade: 0.05), "moisture": (max: 0.45, fade: 0.3)},
        ),
        // Water seeping into a pool underground, wet climate or dry: a thin trickle, near it.
        (
            name: "cave_seep", sound: Stream, volume: 0.14, fade: 4,
            when: {"sky": (max: 0.05, fade: 0.15), "depth": (min: 5, fade: 4), "water": (min: 0.05, fade: 0.05)},
        ),
        // Lava seething and bubbling, near it.
        (
            name: "lava", recording: ["sounds/lava_1.mp3", "sounds/lava_2.mp3", "sounds/lava_3.mp3"], volume: 0.42, fade: 2,
            when: {"lava": (min: 0.35, fade: 0.3)},
        ),
        // Bees about their hive by day: a warm drone by a skep or a wild nest, quiet at
        // night and in the cold, when they keep in, and while it rains.
        (
            name: "bees", sound: Hum, volume: 0.16, fade: 3,
            when: {"hive": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.3), "sun": (min: 0.05, fade: 0.1), "temperature": (min: 10, fade: 4)},
            duck: {"raining": 0.9},
        ),
        // A fire burning close by: a warm low roar and the crackle of the wood, so home
        // sounds lived in. Quiet: it sits under the music.
        (
            name: "fire", sound: Fire, volume: 0.3, fade: 2,
            when: {"fire": (min: 0.6, fade: 0.55)},
        ),
        // The player's own lit hearth, as their home grows round it: a bed of embers glowing
        // under the flames, the coals ticking as they settle. Faint by a bare hearthstone,
        // fuller with each step up the ladder, full in the Heart of the Home.
        (
            name: "embers", sound: Embers, volume: 0.22, fade: 4,
            when: {"fire": (min: 0.6, fade: 0.55), "home": (min: 6, fade: 4.5)},
        ),
        // A kiln firing: a deep roar shut in the brick, the draught howling in its flue.
        (
            name: "kiln_roar", sound: Kiln, volume: 0.32, fade: 2,
            when: {"kiln": (min: 0.6, fade: 0.55)},
        ),
        // An earth clamp burning: a low, close hiss of the logs charring under the soil.
        (
            name: "clamp_hiss", sound: Smoulder, volume: 0.18, fade: 2,
            when: {"clamp": (min: 0.3, fade: 0.25)},
        ),
        // By the hearth on a stormy night: the wind moaning low over the chimney, louder
        // in the gusts.
        (
            name: "flue", sound: Flue, volume: 0.14, fade: 4,
            when: {"fire": (min: 0.6, fade: 0.55), "shelter": (min: 0.6, fade: 0.3), "wind": (min: 10, fade: 6), "sun": (max: 0.05, fade: 0.15)},
        ),
        // The same moan over a lit kiln's stack, heard from shelter by it.
        (
            name: "kiln_flue", sound: Flue, volume: 0.14, fade: 4,
            when: {"kiln": (min: 0.6, fade: 0.55), "shelter": (min: 0.6, fade: 0.3), "wind": (min: 10, fade: 6), "sun": (max: 0.05, fade: 0.15)},
        ),
        // Thatch about to catch: a soft, close sizzle, the warning before the flame (with
        // `smoulder_crackle`'s spits). Only while the server says it smoulders.
        (
